WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.520
andragogy knowles's six assumptions

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:07.040
of adult learners andragogy

3
00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.679
a term popularized in the 1960s by

4
00:00:09.679 --> 00:00:11.040
malcolm knowles

5
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.599
has been defined as the art and science

6
00:00:13.599 --> 00:00:15.599
of teaching adults

7
00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:17.840
knowles developed six assumptions about

8
00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:18.960
adult learners

9
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.119
which has since become a cornerstone for

10
00:00:21.119 --> 00:00:22.080
educators

11
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.480
in designing adult learning content

12
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.800
these six assumptions are

13
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.679
one the need to know two self-concept

14
00:00:31.679 --> 00:00:35.280
three learner experience four

15
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.800
readiness to learn five orientation to

16
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:39.760
learning

17
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.440
and six motivation to learn

18
00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.640
one the need to know

19
00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.640
in order for adults to learn at optimal

20
00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:49.760
efficiency

21
00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.000
they need to understand why they should

22
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.160
learn what you are teaching

23
00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.640
it's best practice to research and ask

24
00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:57.440
students

25
00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.359
what they expect to learn and how this

26
00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:00.800
can benefit them

27
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.879
with that information you can design

28
00:01:02.879 --> 00:01:06.400
much more constructive content for them

29
00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:10.320
two self-concept while younger learners

30
00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:11.920
often need to be guided through the

31
00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:13.439
learning process

32
00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:15.520
adult students are more likely to learn

33
00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:17.119
better if they're able to work

34
00:01:17.119 --> 00:01:20.159
autonomously students should be provided

35
00:01:20.159 --> 00:01:21.920
a collaborative environment

36
00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.840
where a vast amount of their learning is

37
00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:25.280
self-directed

38
00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:27.920
with that in mind it becomes imperative

39
00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.159
that the educator equips the students

40
00:01:30.159 --> 00:01:31.680
with the right tools

41
00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:33.119
and provides the right amount of

42
00:01:33.119 --> 00:01:35.680
instruction so that self-direction has

43
00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:40.560
guidance three learner experience

44
00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.479
adults have a deeper pool of life

45
00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:44.159
experiences to draw from

46
00:01:44.159 --> 00:01:47.040
than younger learners do this influences

47
00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.560
their motivations

48
00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.920
needs interests and goals

49
00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:54.439
as such there's a much greater need for

50
00:01:54.439 --> 00:01:55.759
individualization

51
00:01:55.759 --> 00:01:58.560
within teaching and learning strategies

52
00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.000
it's important therefore

53
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.079
for educators to help learners figure

54
00:02:02.079 --> 00:02:04.159
out their own learning objectives

55
00:02:04.159 --> 00:02:06.240
based on their needs and individual

56
00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:07.439
interests

57
00:02:07.439 --> 00:02:09.598
as well as provide opportunities for

58
00:02:09.598 --> 00:02:12.959
student self-reflection

59
00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:16.640
four readiness to learn while younger

60
00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:17.120
learners

61
00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:18.800
are often taught things that they won't

62
00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.200
utilize until many years later

63
00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.120
adults want to be able to apply what

64
00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.879
they learn to the present

65
00:02:24.879 --> 00:02:27.680
in real life situations courses should

66
00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:28.080
include

67
00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.879
tasks and projects that encourage adult

68
00:02:30.879 --> 00:02:33.040
learners to independently research

69
00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.360
and explore the subject matter and

70
00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:39.440
thereby gaining first-hand experience

71
00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.120
five orientation to learning

72
00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.879
adults are task centered and

73
00:02:44.879 --> 00:02:47.040
problem-centered in their orientation to

74
00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.080
learning

75
00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:50.080
similar to assumption number four

76
00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.160
orientation to learning refers to the

77
00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:54.000
idea that adult learners

78
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.760
want to see how their learning can

79
00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:57.519
address and solve problems

80
00:02:57.519 --> 00:02:59.760
that they regularly face and how it

81
00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:01.680
applies to daily life

82
00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.480
case studies role playing simulations

83
00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:05.920
and self-evaluation

84
00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:09.120
are of great service in this respect

85
00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.959
six motivation to learn for adults

86
00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:16.159
motivation is internal educators need to

87
00:03:16.159 --> 00:03:18.159
take this into consideration when

88
00:03:18.159 --> 00:03:20.080
planning the design and content of their

89
00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:21.280
courses

90
00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:23.200
there must be a valid reason behind each

91
00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.680
activity and learners should understand

92
00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.599
what skills they'll develop by

93
00:03:27.599 --> 00:03:29.840
completing the tasks at hand

94
00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:33.599
relevancy is key as the course develops

95
00:03:33.599 --> 00:03:35.920
educators should evaluate the quality of

96
00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:37.599
the learning experience

97
00:03:37.599 --> 00:03:40.239
and its objectives and reassess learner

98
00:03:40.239 --> 00:03:43.120
needs if necessary

99
00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:44.959
thank you for watching this video i hope

100
00:03:44.959 --> 00:03:46.400
was beneficial

101
00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:53.920
take care

